msgid "LEDs Meaning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-leds-pixhawk.rst:7
#: b834874a017941fa8f4a1ce79b48b713
msgid "This topic explains how to interpret the colours and flash sequence of the main and/or external LED(s), if the :ref:`NTF_LED_OVERRIDE<NTF_LED_OVERRIDE>` parameter is set to its ``standard`` default setting. Some of the LED patterns have associated sound/tone patterns as listed in :ref:`Sounds (Pixhawk) <common-sounds-pixhawkpx4>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-leds-pixhawk.rst:12
#: f770c8e2f94f4f9a9116de9644a1ef74
msgid "Boards with 1 or 2 Notify LEDS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-leds-pixhawk.rst:14
#: 1a040acdde3c4b74a27109a0978edb97
msgid "These boards have one(LED A) or two(LED A and LED B) leds on the board, normally, but not always, green and blue, respectively."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-leds-pixhawk.rst:16
#: cfc4405b31534900a39f09df1dd7ad0d
msgid "After boot, LED A usually shows system status, while LED B shows GPS status. Each sequence of flashes shown below repeats every second. So, LED A will flash with a 50% duty cycle at 4Hz , alternating with LED B, when the autopilot is in ESC calibration mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-leds-pixhawk.rst:18
#: 9c430e314158449aaafd478d1e3240c7
msgid "The states and events are shown in order of precedence. For example, LED A will flash the battery failsafe sequence even if RC is in failsafe also, in the two LED case."
msgstr ""

